From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UebelAndre <github@uebelandre.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:45:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(bazel): take Bazel information from the client

A host that cannot spawn processes (a WebAssembly build, or a sandboxed
one) can run the few Bazel commands the server needs on its behalf and pass
the results in `initializationOptions.bazel`: `bazel info`, the
build-language proto (as a file path) and repository mappings as
`bazel mod dump_repo_mapping` prints them, keyed by canonical repository.

`StaticBazelClient` answers every `BazelClient` call from that data and
reports an error for the operations that would need a live Bazel (fetching
a repository, querying targets). The server picks it whenever the options
carry a `bazel` object and falls back to `BazelCLI` otherwise, so the
native binary accepts the same options, which is how this is tested.
